File Role <code>page-art.js</code> (~20 KB) Draws and animates every picture (page tops once, cards with scroll) (<code>PageArt.init(root)</code>, <code>PageArt.still(subject, aspect, x)</code>) <code>page-art.css</code> (~1 KB) Colours for both themes <code>field2.js</code> (~10 KB) Field generator (<code>Field2.build</code>) <code>art-motion.js</code> (~91 KB) Engine for each subject's working motion (<code>ArtMotion.rig</code>, <code>pose</code>); its web group is hidden by <code>page-art.css</code> <code>subjects.js</code> (~165 KB) The 15 drawn subjects; split per page in production so a page inlines only its own <pre><code>&lt;div class="page-art" data-page-art="software" data-page-art-mode="once"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;  &lt;!-- page top: plays once, stops --&gt;
&lt;div class="page-art" data-page-art="builds" data-page-art-mode="scroll"
     data-page-art-aspect="1.6667"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;                               &lt;!-- card: follows scroll --&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li>The element sizes itself from its <code>aspect-ratio</code>; the picture fills it with   <code>preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"</code>, subject centred. In page headers the element is the   right-hand grid cell of <code>.ph</code> (about 46% of the header width at 1024 px and up), not an absolutely   positioned full-width layer; the text column holds the left side.</li> <li><code>data-page-art-aspect</code>: <code>2</code> (headers and edge pages, default) or <code>1.6667</code> (cards).</li> <li><code>data-page-art-mode</code>: <code>once</code> (page tops and edge pages, default), <code>scroll</code> (cards) or <code>loop</code>   (review pages only; not used on the site).</li> <li>Do not use <code>data-art-motion</code> or call <code>ArtMotion.init</code> on these elements.</li> </ul>

Header Public pages Client pages, shares, API Embeds <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> Strict (below), <code>frame-ancestors 'none'</code> Same Same but <code>frame-ancestors *</code> <code>X-Robots-Tag</code> / meta robots index <code>noindex, nofollow</code> <code>noindex</code> <code>Cache-Control</code> Long, immutable assets <code>no-store</code> Public, short <code>Referrer-Policy</code> <code>strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code> <code>no-referrer</code> <code>no-referrer</code> <code>Strict-Transport-Security</code> <code>max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload</code> Same Same <code>Permissions-Policy</code> camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), … Same Same <code>X-Content-Type-Options</code> <code>nosniff</code> Same Same <code>Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy</code> <code>same-origin</code> Same — <p>CSP (production; report-only for the first week, then enforced):</p> <pre><code>default-src 'self';
script-src 'self' 'nonce-…' 'strict-dynamic' https://challenges.cloudflare.com;
style-src 'self';
img-src 'self' data: blob: https://media.&lt;domain&gt; https://&lt;private-r2-host&gt;;
media-src 'self' https://media.&lt;domain&gt; https://&lt;private-r2-host&gt;;
font-src 'self';
connect-src 'self' https://&lt;private-r2-host&gt;;
frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com;
base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none';
require-trusted-types-for 'script';
</code></pre> <p>Because the link cookie is readable by script, XSS is the main risk to a link. The defences are this CSP (no inline scripts, no third-party scripts except Turnstile), Trusted Types, React's escaping, no <code>dangerouslySetInnerHTML</code> outside the MDX pipeline, and no user content rendered as HTML anywhere in the client area.</p>
